From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 06:18:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Remove the last AxisAlignedBB and light-propagation
 allocations

c() was still calling the BlockPosition form of getRawLight for its two seed
reads, and that form shifted a fresh position per direction and copied
EnumDirection.values() on every call - 55 MB/min. Taking the coordinates a few
lines earlier lets both reads use the scalar form, which left the BlockPosition
version with no callers; a second copy of the propagation rule would only have
drifted, so it is deleted. markBlocksDirtyVertical gets a coordinate updateLight
rather than building a position per Y level.

pushOutOfBlocks was the last source of AxisAlignedBB in the server, by two
separate routes. Its collision-box list was only ever tested for emptiness, so
hasCollisionBoxes gathers into the shared sink and stops at the first box; and
isBlockFullCube built a whole box to read getAverageEdgeLength off it, six times
per tick for every dropped item and experience orb. EntityLiving's teleport
search used the list the same way and switches over too.

isBlockFullCube can be reached from inside a sink gather, so it takes a scratch
slot and a bounds buffer of its own rather than borrowing the sink's - sharing
either would corrupt the enclosing query. hasCollisionBoxes relies on every
multi-box block having moved to addCollisionBoxes: a block still overriding only
addCollisionBoxesToList would report no collision at all, so that was checked -
the legacy override exists nowhere but Block itself.

EnumDirection.random() called values() twice, copying the array twice per call,
and BlockFluids.checkForMixing copied it once and shifted six positions.

